          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దోమ (dōma) — \"a mosquito\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దోమ (dōma) is a mosquito. The word is inherited, and it is said with feeling."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A దోమ (dōma) is the reason for the net over a bed, for smoke at dusk, and for half the complaints of a hot సాయంత్రం."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is also the standard small annoyance. Somebody waving away a threat calls it a దోమ (dōma), and somebody who could not sleep blames one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three. The smallest of them and the loudest complaint."
            }
          ]
        },
