          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఉడుత (uḍuta) — \"a squirrel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఉడుత (uḍuta) is a squirrel — the striped palm squirrel that runs along the top of a గోడ and out onto any కొమ్మ it can reach."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is inherited. The three stripes down its back carry a story that every Telugu household can tell, and the animal is let alone because of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An ఉడుత (uḍuta)'s help is a set phrase for a small contribution offered honestly. Whoever says it is calling their own share tiny and means to give it anyway."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four. The one nobody chases off."
            }
          ]
        },
