          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాలీడు (sālīḍu) — \"a spider\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాలీడు (sālīḍu) is a spider — the one in the corner where the గోడ meets the కప్పు."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is inherited, and it is built on the old Telugu word for a weaver, so the name says what the creature does. The thread a person works with is దారం, which you already have."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ask whether one has been swept out and the answer is a plain అవును or లేదు, which is where five small creatures have got you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: ఎలుక (eluka), కప్ప (kappa), దోమ (dōma), ఉడుత (uḍuta), సాలీడు (sālīḍu). Everything small enough to share a house with."
            }
          ]
        },
